## Context

From `conception/2026-11-01-dsh-superagent-ideas.md` § 2. dsh-superagent
refuses to infer "waiting on a person" from free text: an agent that needs a
decision fills one structured `human_action` field with one question, and
the panel lists those first. Here, author questions are spread across
ticket logs, PR comments and chat, which makes "one at a time, queue the
rest" (`rules/workflow.md` § Autonomous action) hard to check.

## Author remark (2026-11-01)

Adding headers to erg is very expensive. Explore other implementation
routes before proposing one.

Routes to compare, cost and failure mode for each (not exhaustive):

- the existing `needs-human` label (`tickets/.ergrc`) plus a log-line
  convention carrying the one question (`<ts> <author> ask <question>`),
  read by `/dashboard`;
- a body section (`## Question for the author`) found by grep;
- a GitHub PR label or review state, for questions raised on a PR;
- a single queue file outside tickets (and why it would or would not drift);
- dashboard-only: derive the list from what exists today, no new writes.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Routes compared in a short note (cost to implement, cost per use, how it drifts, what reads it); no erg format change unless every other route fails, with that argued
- [ ] The author picks a route
- [ ] `/dashboard` lists what waits on the author first, each with its one question, and prints nothing for that section when nothing waits
